[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Creator holding a ping-pong paddle, introducing the video.
AUDIO: 'Today, we\'re making a full explainer video just for practice, starting with a 30-second voiceover script. Then, the main character concept, step three, 3D product renders on green screen, step four, environments and fully structured'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scenes. In each step, there\'s a ping-pong happening between After Effects and FlashBoards, passing shots back and forth until every scene works. Before we start, please take a look. See'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this little guy? Adorable, right? Wrong. He\'s obsessed with money. My guy built his store overnight. Anti-gravity mug? The coffee escapes? Moon toaster? That is a rock. A chair? We don\'t know'

[00:38] [scene:result]
VISUAL: Final explainer video showing "agancy name" and "we make weird sell!".
AUDIO: 'what that chair does. Nobody does. Fishbowl blender? Telepathic pillow? Rocket kettle? Rocket fan? He sold nothing. Zero.'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Nada. Then he showed up at our door, and suddenly, items are filling customers\' carts. Sky is raining money. Three galaxies, one famous little guy. What are you waiting for? We make weird sell.'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The concept, an alien entrepreneur who keeps failing with absurd products until he gets help from a creative agency. The rule I set for myself, AI generates, but the pipeline stays mine. Every decision'

[01:15] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI showing a 3D alien character generated by Nano Banana 2, with prompt details.
AUDIO: 'about timing, composition, and comedy still happens in the tools I already know. Pro tip, write the script before touching any AI tool because generating visuals and writing around them is how'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you end up with beautiful footage that doesn\'t cut together. Let\'s start with the character concept. I simply asked Claude, "Make me a nano banana." Prompt for a cute alien with glasses. I'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generated it in FlashBoards, and here\'s the first concept. A good start. I didn\'t like the legs and hands, so I started building on what I already had. And since every prompt I use stays'

[01:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'available inside FlashBoards, let\'s focus on the process. I removed the legs and hands, made a flat 2D version, and made the glasses a solid color. This version isn\'t for the video. It\'s a'

[02:03] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI displaying a 2D version of the alien character.
AUDIO: 'simpler reference for After Effects to build a reference animation that will render later in C Dance 2. Now, continuing with the stylized version, and this is the final concept. From'

[02:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this, I\'m going to make him sad. Then thinking about money. Then make him morph into a search bar. I had three options, and I chose this one.'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And I added an anti-gravity mug inside it. Now our scenes are ready for the first portion of the script, because I\'m always thinking and generating with the main script in mind. From here, I\'m moving to animation in After Effects.'

[02:42] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: After Effects UI showing the alien character being animated with shape layers and puppet tools.
AUDIO: 'Remember the 2D version? I simply used it as a perfect reference to redraw him with After Effects shape layers. Then I animated everything the way I wanted. Blobby animation for the body,'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and some puppet tool for his little two things here. Then he gets sad, and I used this image as the reference for the thinking bubble.'

[03:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Redraw everything with shape layers. Animate it. Then a cool morphing animation from everything I have into the search bar. Now that I have my first high-contrast'

[03:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'animation guide, I moved back to flash boards. Using the animation guide and selecting the three references I had, all on the same black screen, I asked C Dance to re-render every frame of the'

[03:31] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI with multiple generated images from Nano Banana 2, including character variations and orbs.
AUDIO: 'guide into the same style and look dev as the stylized references. I got two options. And this one works better for me.'

[03:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But before heading back to After Effects, I need a background. So, I extracted this background from an earlier concept and asked Nano banana 2D generate some cool 3D stylized orbs to make things prettier in the compositing'

[03:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'process. Now that I have everything I need, moving back to After Effects. Here we have the footage in After Effects and the first thing we need is to remove the background. I could do that in C dance too, but it\'s a very easy fix in After'

[04:11] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: After Effects UI showing compositing of the animated alien with a thought bubble and background orbs.
AUDIO: 'Effects. So, why waste a couple of dollars when I can do it in one click? I\'m going to use the roto brush in After Effects. Double click on the footage first. Select the roto brush tool and simply click the'

[04:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'object. And just like that, the background is gone and the object stays vibrant. Go back to the roto brush to add or remove parts of the footage whenever needed.'

[04:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And once you\'re satisfied with the result, bring the shift edge all the way down to minus 100. This softens the edges and removes any black remains. Moving on to the background we extracted'

[04:47] [scene:promo]
VISUAL: On-screen text "10% OFF FIRST SUBSCRIPTION TOP-UPS" with a cartoon character.
AUDIO: 'earlier, I added two of those orbs key lighted with a fast box blur floating in the foreground. Then I duplicated the main footage with a fill, a blur, and an overlay blending mode. And our first'

[04:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'portion is locked and ready. Everything you just saw done in less than an hour because combining AI with your workflow is a real boost in speed and productivity with some really great results. Great news! Flashboards is'

[05:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'offering 10% off on your first subscription and top up. The coupon code is flash 10. Don\'t miss the opportunity. The link is in the description. Let\'s continue with the next portion. Generating weird alien 3D objects. I'

[05:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'started by asking Claude this, "Make me Nano banana prompts to generate 12 weird products for sale straight out of imagination from the cute aliens world 3D products with a cool modern soft'

[05:37] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI displaying a grid of 3D product renders generated by Nano Banana 2, mostly on green screens.
AUDIO: 'style." And Claude gave me the 12 prompts for the 12 products. So, I I to Flashboards and generated every single one of them. Chose the best option for each, made sure everyone sits on a solid'

[05:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'green background for keying later. Then upscaled all of them for C Dance 2 Omni and generated a perfect looping 3D rotation for every single one. Now, I want to place these products in'

[06:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'some sort of digital store. So, I need every product to sit on an e-commerce shopping card. I took the anti-gravity mug and asked Nano Banana 2 to make an e-commerce product card UI'

[06:15] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI showing a video playback of a 3D product (a phone-like device) with a green background, generated by Kling AI.
AUDIO: 'with the product name, the price, and an add to cart button. Then I kept editing the generated results until I got this plain card with only the button and a coin symbol. Made it float solo on a green background.'

[06:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then I made a very simple high-contrast UI animation for it in After Effects. Nothing too fancy. And lastly, with C Dance 2 Omni, I re-rendered it on the same green screen. And now we have all'

[06:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the products and a soft 3D card rendered for each one of them. Back into After Effects now. Here, I have all the products arranged in compositions, roto brushed, and perfectly looped for around'

[06:54] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: After Effects UI showing multiple 3D product cards being arranged and composited.
AUDIO: '20 seconds to fit the whole voice-over portion. Then, in the main composition, I brought everything into one big 4K comp, every product and every card with some custom handwritten text layers made'

[07:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in After Effects to make things prettier for each and every product. Offsetting them while they\'re on screen, of course, and with some orbs floating here and there. This one, for instance, is a transparent orb with an adjustment layer switched on running a CC lens effect, so'

[07:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it distorts everything underneath it like a water drop. And some other orbs with blur to add depth. And in the main composition, I moved the whole 4K comp with position keyframes emulating a'

[07:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera traveling from one card to the next following the voice-over, anti-gravity mug, moon toaster, weird chair, and so on. Can you guess how fast all of this got done? This is insane. Do the math and'

[07:46] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI with various generated images, including sad alien expressions, crying faces, and warehouse environments.
AUDIO: 'let me know in the comments how much time it would take to do just the modeling for each and every object. For me, it took literally minutes. Now moving on, he sold nothing. I made him'

[07:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stand sad in an empty warehouse. Next scene, the sad guy along with this simple crying face and a zero smashing his little warehouse and the alien is crying out loud.'

[08:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The next scene is here. I didn\'t want the floating eyebrows, so I removed them. Then, using C Dance to Omni, I animated both scenes. Two tries and honestly, both are'

[08:24] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI showing a "BUY NOW" button with a spider, generated by Nano Banana 2.
AUDIO: 'perfect. Then, when the voice over says nada, I made this buy now button with a spider living on it, but I wanted the'

[08:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'transition from the crying scene into this one to be seamless. So, I made a simple animation for the button in After Effects and this time I asked C Dance to follow the reference as usual, but to animate the spider hanging physically,'

[08:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'perfectly synced with the button\'s animation. And surprisingly, the results are amazing. I chose this one because there\'s a slight offset in the spider\'s legs'

[09:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'animation and those kinds of details make a real difference in quality. Then, in After Effects, I placed the new scenes under the product cards to make everything seamless with no cuts or any'

[09:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uncomfortable transitions and the spider button acts as a mask for the crying scene. And now, everything is connected perfectly. Since I\'m the director of my own work, I control when and where to'

[09:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'use AI. And with After Effects compositing, I made sure everything connects seamlessly. Moving on from the spider buy now button, this is the most complex scene in this whole fun project.'

[09:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I wanted to test whether C-Dance could handle re-rendering this line morphing animation into the shopping cart. So, first I made a shopping cart icon concept. Then, with the high contrast animation guide from After Effects, I'

[09:52] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI showing a video playback of a star animation.
AUDIO: 'asked C-Dance 2 Omni to re-render the animation in the shopping cart style. Three tries. This one is bad. This one is good. But, there\'s a red line. And this one is perfect.'

[10:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, that\'s the one I chose. And of course, we can\'t leave our spider friend hanging there for too long. So, I added this animation from an old project. Extracted a frame out of it, restyled it'

[10:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with Nano Banana 2, removed the big star, and rendered it with C-Dance 2. The first try, not good. But, the second one is perfect.'

[10:29] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: After Effects UI showing the compositing of the spider button and other elements.
AUDIO: 'And it even adds extra motion to the right. Exactly where the lines are headed. Making it a perfect transition. I really enjoyed compositing this one. Here\'s the spider button. I started by'

[10:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'adding the star scene. Then, since this shopping cart line morphing animation happens in a wide comp, I animated its position moving outward to emulate that camera movement. I linked the spider button as a child to this wide comp, so'

[10:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it moves along with it. Then, the main lines footage roto brushed multiple times to extract each stroke on its own. I placed some strokes above the spider button and some below to create a more believable sense of depth. Then, the'

[11:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'number counter, a very simple animation. And last but not least, the same 3D objects trick. I made a looped 3D shopping cart icon to make everything more beautiful and push it toward that'

[11:20] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'premium side of animation. And just like that, it\'s ready. The workflow so far? A joyful game of ping pong. Like I\'ve grown eight arms, each one doing something different. And they\'re all handing me pieces to combine. That\'s the'

[11:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'real modern workflow. Now, the final scenes. It\'s raining money now, so let\'s make it happen. I asked Nano Banana first to make it rain alien coins and cash on our little fellow. The'

[11:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'result? Bad. So, I edited it. Better, but now the body shape changed. So, keep everything, change only the body shape. Then, three tries in Sea Dance 2 to make it really rain with the'

[11:58] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: After Effects UI showing a shopping cart animation.
AUDIO: 'coins and money moving right. And here we have it. But, this is a full frame scene, and we left off on a tiny shopping cart icon. How do we pull off a cool seamless'

[12:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'transition? Easy. Since it\'s raining money, let\'s make a 3D coin rotating naturally in a perfect loop. Then, a money bill flying in and out of the scene. And in After Effects, I roto brushed the'

[12:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'coin footage and rotated it 90° so it now spins horizontally. Then made it fall and cover the entire previous scene, revealing the new one. And for the out animation, the money'

[12:35] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Flashboards UI displaying multiple generated galaxy concepts with alien statues.
AUDIO: 'bill does the same trick. Flies in to cover the scene. Flies out to reveal the next one. How cool is that? From the same environment, we reused elements to keep everything seamless throughout the whole project. And now,'

[12:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the final outro scenes, our famous guy in three different galaxies. First, I made three galaxy concepts with statues of our little fellow standing across all'

[13:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'three. Then, I simply asked Sea Dance 2 Omni to orbit the camera 360° around every statue so I could do match cut transitions later in After Effects. And here\'s every chosen try. Since'

[13:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything will be available in Flashboards, I\'m not showing you every single result. And of course, I\'m not showing you the prices, either. Go to Flashboards and find them yourself. You\'ll be shocked. And now, back into After Effects one'

[13:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'last time for some time-remapped match cuts between the three Galaxies. And just like that, the whole project is done. To access this project\'s board, head to'

[13:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'flashboards. You\'ll find it right here in boards along with all our other videos and project boards. One click away and you\'re exploring tons of prompts and results. AI didn\'t replace my workflow, it plugged into it.'

[13:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The speed is AI, but the taste and the decisions still all yours. If you enjoyed this, drop a like and subscribe. Keep experimenting and see you in the next one.'
